    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d309-a9">

                <pb facs="0513" n="443" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg443"/>

                <head>Mr. Otterbourg to M.
                        Dano</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States in
                                Mexico,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-07-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 23, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister:</hi> In reply to the request you made
                    of me, on the 17th instant, according to custom, for information respecting
                    formalities to be observed in quitting Mexico, I have the honor to inform you
                    that I learn from Mr. Lerdo de Tejada himself that your object cannot be
                    obtained without addressing him directly.</p>
                <p>Accept, Mr. Minister, the assurance of my distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>MARCUS OTTERBOURG, <hi rendition="#italic">Envoy Extraordinary and
                            Minister Plenipotentiary of the United States of America in
                        Mexico.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">M. Alphonse Dano,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Envoy Extraordinary and Minister Plenipotentiary of
                            France in Mexico.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
